content:
@BenWestgate_ @Abuamerican Not tried Sema but Tirzepatide nuked my appetite beyond comprehension. 

Game changer for obese people but if you’re relatively fit just wanting a cheat code it’s not worth it 

Struggled to eat 800 cals per day

@RockAppleWood @DoctorTro Was keto for 4 plus years. Intermittent fasting as well. Weight and A1c continued to creep. 
Eating the same now. But with mounjaro. Down 65 pounds. 
Also sleeping thru the night for the first time in a decade. Another bonus.

@DrBrandonPettke Yesterday I watched a Youtube video on how Charles Barkley lost so much weight through intermittent fasting and the drug Mounjaro.

I was so intrigued and planned to research it in detail later.

Thanks for this thread Dr. You saved me from that work and shared good advice.

"This is not a quick fix for a celebrity looking to lose ten pounds," @kavitapmd says of new diabetes drug tirzepatide, aka Mounjaro. 

"These drugs are a life changer and truly a life saver for my diabetic patients."

@jdbalart 
@MSNBC https://t.co/mcdV7PdVyf

@thatsnotmine125 @ProfKarolSikora I am referring to the type 2 diabetes medication (that's all the rave now) used for curbing appetite.

That specific use needs to be maintained.  Once stopped, weight gain comes right back.

Some of drugs are Ozempic and Mounjaro as examples.

@FatEmperor 

Nationwide shortage of drugs like Mounjaro, Ozempic, etc. Why aren't doctors prescribing no carb?

I've lost more weight (I was NEVER obese) faster, healthier, &amp; cheaper than ANY of my patients on these "wonder" injections by going BBBE (beef, bacon, butter, &amp;eggs).

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/rlYXC7ZWsb

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/UpKoGdpnvH

@RuxandraTeslo I lost 40lb on tirzepatide (Mounjaro)

Idk why there are so many haters tbh, I don’t lie about it

Anytime anyone asks me I’m very honest that I just take a drug and it works, I don’t do “stolen valor” fitness edition claiming some other account of the weight loss

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/9rJ11Y6tml

@723Magnus @biodiversityge1 I was put on Mounjaro for type2 diabetes in August 
It was $1200.00 with my insurance bc of my high deductible. I changed insurance policies  bc I’ll be on this for life. Now it’s 20 dollars. My sugars are controlled , my A1c is almost normal. 
and I’ve lost 28 pounds 18weeks https://t.co/Dn09l4Cy86

@ScottAdamsSays Mounjaro. Just started dose course Saturday. Preliminary indications are promising. Glucose levels are more stable than Ozempic meaning no up and down glucose spiking.   
  My appetite is also stabilized meaning no urgent hunger pains. 
  No GI distress so far.

@DefiningWealth I ate 1400 cals a day for year and only gained.

I have thyroid disease, PCOS, and PPMD, all which cause weight gain.

Started taking Mounjaro and it’s been a lifesaver. I’m now down 15 pounds, with the same habits I had before.

@KayannaStardust @SilverSapphire9 Same!
The only reason I've been able to qualify for mounjaro is because I'm technically type 1 and type 2. 

It's been wonders for my sugar levels and appetite. I went from using 150 units ever 3 days to needing about 60 units every 3 days in my pod.

@StockMKTNewz As someone in healthcare, This is not surprising. Eli Lilly has been successful with it’s insulin offerings

And now, it has a blockbuster in weight loss in MOUNJARO. 

We cannot stay stocked on mounjaro. And patients come back and tell me they have lost 15-30% total weight.

@dtex1961 @bagsfan75_Tony Good. Metformin made sure that I was a "regular" guy. Ask your doc about the Mounjaro. It doesn't get any easier than that. And at $25/month, it's plumb cheap.
While I was in the hospital they were poking my fingers all the time.
If I send you a DM, open it. I'm having a thought.

@voidkitten_ @bbumobx @LizTweetsThings I was an insulin dependent diabetic, was... 

taking Mounjaro means my blood sugar remains 100 most of the day. No more insulin.

Would you rather inject yourself 4-6 times a day, and still not have great control? Or once a week and excellent control?

A new drug sold under the brand name Mounjaro and taken once a week may soon be approved to treat obesity. 

Currently used to treat Type 2 diabetes, research suggests it could help people shed large amounts of fat. 

@DrAmirKhanGP explains. https://t.co/wAU4hSgSrW

TONIGHT ON #NIGHTLINE: Mounjaro could soon be FDA approved for weight loss. 

Currently the medication is used to treat Type 2 diabetes, but its manufacturer released data last week that they say demonstrates the drug is safe and effective for weight loss. 

@MonaKAbdi has more. https://t.co/LlN6SNHpPm

Eli Lilly kicks off consumer campaign for diabetes drug Mounjaro 

@LillyPad's campaign comes weeks after Mounjaro returned to shelves following a two-month shortage, via @MMMnews 

https://t.co/w0tvF46WwQ

Tirzapatide is a new class of medication for diabetes and soon for obesity. An amazing group develop this systematic review. Take a look. Thanks @EndoSocJournals for the publication

https://t.co/ylZ8MgNRTU

@TheEndoSociety @EndoConnect @Endocrine_News @EndocrineToday

@emmarcourt The real issue in my mind is how the pharmaceutical industry is pricing these drugs.

#Wegovy is $1350 per month while Ozempic, is $925. Hope @LillyPad doesn’t follow suit with #Mounjaro 

@novonordiskus Nordisk is penalizing people with obesity by charging 45% more!

@comeonandfarce (maybe I missed this part of your coverage) 
Tirzepatide is approved for type II diabetes. There are shortages for diabetics trying to get this drug because so many people are using to it off label for weight loss. 
2 people in my family affected by this

@SullyCNBC @LastCallCNBC $LLY
1. Life changing drug Mounjaro/Zepbound 
2. up 50%+ and only just getting started.

@OptionsMike Have a good night. Slow day for the most part.
$LLY slid after data from Mounjaro study showed people did lose 20% of body weight during trial but regained 15% of body weight over the next year after no longer using drug. Looks like overreaction in $LLY to me.
CPI in the am.

What do you think about a 5 day fast assisted with tirzepatide?

How does using strong GLP-1 agonist impact fasting?

@DragonBowtied @BowTiedUM @Denis_protocol

@MounjaroHCP WHY is Mounjaro so expensive? 
I’m in tears leaving Walgreens (without my prescription) after being told I needed to pay $896 for a 1-month dose. 
I didn’t ask to be a Type 2 diabetic, but who in the world can pay that? That’s just pure greed.

@NMoonitz I'm going to answer you totally honestly:

I did most of it using a combo of low carb and low calorie, but at 200 I hit a wall that wouldn't move no matter what bc of PCOS and an underactive thyroid, so I went on Mounjaro. It's made all the difference.

Most was organic though.

@BowTiedBull If they ban it they'll sell more Mounjaro 

Then they'll ban Mounjaro to sell Retatrutide when that's approved etc

Not a bad thing for the morbidly obese or professional bbers using it to cut instead of clen, ephedrine, addy etc.

@CouchGnome @whosthatsquish @Brain_On_FireTX @TheMcKenziest @SmithCkilg MANY ppl are using Ozempic or Mounjaro &amp; don't actually need it... hence the "side effect" of the neck skin thing 😅
I've seen too many pts that are within a healthy weight range (&amp; are NOT type 2 diabetic) getting these meds.
That's where the fat phobia comes in.
